---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import { outsideOfWork } from '../data/resume';
---

<Base
  title="About — Pranav Gillella"
  description="Carrollton, Texas to UIUC. Why I'm studying finance and computer science together, and what I'm building toward."
>
  <Section title="About" as="h1" gap="tight">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I grew up in Carrollton, Texas, and I'm a freshman at the University of
        Illinois — finance in Gies, computer science minor in Grainger.
      </p>
      <p>
        Markets came first. In 2023 I won the Stock Market Game and was a
        national finalist in InvestWrite, and what stuck was not the winning. It
        was that a written argument about a company could be checked against
        what actually happened afterward. Code came second, through AP Computer
        Science, and it took me a while to notice the two were the same
        instinct: make the claim, then find out whether you were right.
      </p>
      <p>
        That's why I'm doing both rather than picking one. Finance without
        programming means taking someone else's numbers on faith. Programming
        without finance means building tools with no view about what's worth
        measuring.
      </p>
      <p>
        I run Quant Labs LLC, which is two products I built and operate alone.
        EarlyDMV rebooks Texas DPS driver license appointments into earlier
        slots. Protestly files property tax protests for Denton County
        homeowners and argues them at the appraisal review board. Both are live,
        both have paying customers, and both are hosted on hardware I manage
        myself.
      </p>
      <p>
        What I'm working toward is quant research or trading. The <a
          href="/projects/ma-crossover-backtest">backtester</a
        > is where that starts — I wrote the metrics from scratch specifically so
        I'd understand what they hide.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Outside of work" gap="tight">
    <ul class="plain">
      {outsideOfWork.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section gap="tight">
    {/* A sentence, so the links keep their underlines. */}
    <p class="prose">
      More detail on <a href="/experience">experience and skills</a>, or the <a
        href="/resume">résumé</a
      >.
    </p>
  </Section>
</Base>
